<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Oda regime</h1><p class="st-meta">1559 CE – 1582 CE · capital Azuchi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The regime of Oda Nobunaga, the warlord who began the unification of Japan, broke the power of Buddhist armies and built the castle of Azuchi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> inherited part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owari-province">Owari</a> in 1551 and had united the province by 1559. His surprise victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-yoshimoto">Imagawa Yoshimoto</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okehazama">Okehazama</a> in 1560 made his name, and he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mino-province">Mino</a> in 1567, adopting a seal proclaiming rule of the realm by force.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1568 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Nobunaga</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshiaki">Ashikaga Yoshiaki</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>, then expelled him in 1573. He burned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enryaku-ji">Enryaku-ji</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-hiei">Mount Hiei</a> in 1571, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-clan">Takeda</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nagashino">Nagashino</a> in 1575 with massed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ishiyama-hongan-ji">Ishiyama Hongan-ji</a> until 1580. He abolished toll barriers, created free markets, tolerated Christian missionaries and built Azuchi castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-biwa">Lake Biwa</a> from 1576.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1582 his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akechi-mitsuhide">Akechi Mitsuhide</a> attacked him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honno-ji">Honno-ji</a> temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Nobunaga</a> died; his heir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobutada">Nobutada</a> was also killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> defeated Mitsuhide and took over the regime.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1559 CE – 1582 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Korea and Japan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.73%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1559 CE – 1582 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Azuchi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Oda Nobunaga, Oda Nobutada</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oda clan domain, Oda Nobunaga's regime, Azuchi regime</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1570&amp;focus=oda-regime" aria-label="Oda regime on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8128 907 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Oda regime lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8448 1163L8441 1168M8448 1163L8441 1178M8448 1163L8442 1182M8448 1163L8440 1178M8448 1163L8500 1145M8448 1163L8436 1134M8448 1163L8445 1152M8448 1163L8478 1169"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8441 1168h0M8441 1178h0M8442 1182h0M8440 1178h0M8500 1145h0M8436 1134h0M8445 1152h0M8478 1169h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8448 1163h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8448 1163h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot mar